<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic618249c235504421c2e20ea7f827c43fbe68f1d" commit="587135cbf004cbec20787ad180e0915ba042223b" commit_message="Added a Monarch metrics collector  - Added a small wrapper lib/ts_mon_config which sets up the global   singleton collector without adding the noisy command line flags from   ts_mon's config.add_argparse_options  BUG=chromium:573323 TEST=Imports work  Change-Id: Ic618249c235504421c2e20ea7f827c43fbe68f1d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319638 Commit-Ready: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319638" owner_email="phobbs@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/38/319638/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0736bdf785835d60f87b87f3a1d00cb4e5b6c488" commit="8e8c07df18239eb87348f893e19727ca6e9cae58" commit_message="sync_stages: Added Monarch metrics collection.  Added some stats collection via Monarch in parallel to the statsd collection in the pre-cq stage.  TEST=sync_stages_unittest BUG=chromium:573323  Change-Id: I0736bdf785835d60f87b87f3a1d00cb4e5b6c488 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319639 Commit-Ready: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319639" owner_email="phobbs@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/39/319639/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1be6b3c7f3a780bff343e32333ba790f42ad09b8" commit="f8d7fe7063232036f1e62ceea4359ecb0d3da04d" commit_message="bundle_firmware: limit size of CBFS for RW slots  Now that boards are switched over to a CBFS in each RW slot the hashing taking place is a lot more than the component method. The reason is that 1. there's more things within the CBFS 2. the RW slots weren't always fully utilized. To gain back more boot speed limit the size of the CBFS that is hashed in the RW slots.  This is accomplished by taking advatage of the cbfstool 'compact' command which removes empty file fragmentation from CBFS regions. This command is invoked for nodes which contin a cbfs-files subnode. Additionally, the cbfstool 'print' command is ran with a parseable option which allows limiting the CBFS region to be hashed by changing the size of the region to the offset of the last file if it is empty. i.e. if the last file entry is empty there's no need to include it in the hashed data.  Lastly, there's no reason to include a master header within the RW slots so remove that as well.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49764 BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=glados CQ-DEPEND=CL:324094,CL:324095 TEST=Built and booted chell with cbfstool and dev-util patches.  Change-Id: I1be6b3c7f3a780bff343e32333ba790f42ad09b8 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324023 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324023" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/23/324023/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6c1eae7d9348197b736af125667604eeb7239c92" commit="202d59f6c40cf421e067f882afd027ab3005de74" commit_message="arc-build.eclass: add clang support  BUG=None TEST=building hello world w/clang &amp; clang++ works now  Change-Id: I6c1eae7d9348197b736af125667604eeb7239c92 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324430 Comm